I have been playing nethack for quite a while now and finally after many
unsuccessful games I got to a happy ending. This was
the second game where I got past Medusa and my first game where I got 
past the castle.








SPOILER WARNING:

I read a lot of spoilers and I guess this post contains spoily
details as well.












This game started as a protection run. Robbing two shops with the help
of my cat Lucius gave me enough money and some spells. My armor was not
good at this point, but I couldn't improve it and I still went down into
the mines. In the mines my hitpoints once dropped to 1 and I had a
narrow escape. I reached gnome town with my experience level still at 1.
I spent my money at the temple and got an intrinsic armor class of 1. I
started leveling up now. I was level 2 when my large cat attacked the
watch captain and got killed, I continued petless.

The Sokoban tower contained the amulet of reflection, which was a
disapointment for me as I hoped for the bag of holding.

Two levels above sokoban there was a neutral altar (level 7). My first
sacrifice in this game was a crocodile. I recieved Magicbane. Lacking a
bag of holding I set up my stash there.

The game continued smoothly for a while without anything significant 
happening. My first prayer on the altar for blessing water crowned me 
and gave me the finger of death spell.

The quest was easy. I defeated the Dark One using Magicbane.

The portal to Fort Ludius was on level 22. I didn't empty it, but went 
further to the castle. I turned back and searched the dungeons for more 
items. Later I wanted to return and used the Eye of the Aethiopica to 
teleport me to Fort Ludius. Oh! I noticed that I did not get teleported 
to the entry, instead I landed inside the level, which was still full 
with soldiers and worse creatures. I was close to some door in the nord 
west. I opened the door and used the room as a defense while defeating 
one soldier after the other. A silver dragon also attacked me and when I 
defeated it, it left behind a set of scales! So my +1 leather jacket 
soon got replaced by a +1 silver dragon scale mail.

I went into the Valley of the Dead and returned to empty the caste. I 
continued descending down into Gehennom. In the first level below the 
Valley of the Dead was Asmodeus. I didn't pay him, but noticed that I 
was not experienced in fighting demons. Asmodeus summond Dispatcher and 
I had a long and hard battle against them. I used a lot of potions of 
full healing.

The rest of Gehennom was easy after that. My main problem was that I 
still lacked a bag of holding. I didn't pick up any gold. I defeated 
Vlad and finally found the vibrating square.

I returned to my stash for the last preparations. I quaffed my two 
blessed smoky potions of restore ability, but they didn't give me a 
wish. I rubbed one of my two magic lamps, I used the two charges from 
the castle wand. Speed boots, bag of holding, helm of brilliance. I 
wrote a lot of scrolls of enchant armor, recharged the castle wand and 
went down again.

The Wizard of Yendor never got a chance to attack me. Finger of death is 
a nice spell. In his tower the game finally gave me a bag of holding. If 
it had done so before I would have needed one wish less. I went to the 
sanctum. There somehow a curse hit me even though I was wielding 
Magicbane. I was blind at the time. My dragon scale mail lost the 
blessing, my lizard corpse got cursed.

Escaping Gehennom with the Amulet of Yendor was not quite interesting as 
I had to go through the same levels several times.

I entered the planes. After using the confused scroll method to find the 
portal I dug my way using wands of digging. One time I tryed using a 
pickaxe but got hit with a curse. Magicbane wasn't active now and so my 
cloak of magic resistance lost the blessing, my wand of death got cursed.

The air elementals were not so nice, I got sucked into some of them and 
they did a lot of damage. I broke out of them using the finger of death 
and escaped to the portal.

Astral was harder than I imagined. My guardian angel soon died and I was 
unable to fight the hostile angels. The Amulet of Yendor made 
spellcasting almost impossible and the angels were very fast in melee 
combat. On #nethack I got the advice to teleport them away.

Famine got defeated twice by the cursed wand of death. I was lucky and 
the first altar was neutral. #offer. End.


